spans.s:
सम्-अभि-√ धा p. -दधाति, to speak to, address (acc.), Kathās.;
to proclaim, announce, Kir.;
to direct all one's thoughts to (acc.), MW.

सम्-अभि-√ पद् Ā. -पद्यते, to come to, arrive at, attain (acc.), MBh.;
to get one's reward, ib.;
to reply, answer, ib.

सम्-अभि-√ वृत् Ā. -वर्तते, to go towards, advance, MBh.;
to attack, assail, Hariv.;
to come near, approach, MBh.;
to turn back, return, recur, Suśr.;
to remain, continue (तूष्णीम्, ‘silent’), R.;
 w.r. for सम्-अति-√ वृत्.

(-अभि-√ इ) P. -अभ्य्-एति, to go towards, come near, approach, RV.; R. &c.;
to accrue to (acc.), MārkP.;
to follow, attend, wait upon, Śiś.
